      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e So it incorrectly enters the guest which is in a broken state,\n\nI was reading the bug and it mentions about a live lock instead of entering the guest. From reading the code, I think that is true. if pKVM doesn\u0027t handle the event in `__pkvm_vcpu_enter_guest`, then it may return 1 and cause an unbounded for loop live lock in `pkvm_vcpu_enter_guest`. There is a case where we will not return 1 - if `force_immediate_exit` is true and that happens only with `KVM_RUN_FORCE_IMMEDIATE_EXIT` which doesn\u0027t seem to be set for pVMs. The other case for `req_immediate_exit` to be true is via `kvm_check_and_inject_events` but that only for nested which we don\u0027t support.\n\nIs my understanding correct?",
      "revId": "a944ee0243c8a94907a9dcb8b362f9e279de1731",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
