      "writtenOn": "2026-10-01T14:50:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was wondering if there are more events that we don\u0027t check in pKVM and may lead to live lock? If we don\u0027t process it in here, we would return 1 in this function and then live locks in the for loop in `pkvm_vcpu_enter_guest`:\n```\n»       for (;;) {\n»       »       ret \u003d __pkvm_vcpu_enter_guest(vcpu, force_immediate_exit);\n»       »       if (ret \u003c\u003d 0) \n»       »       »       break;\n»       }\n```\n\nIf there might be more events, would it be better to check it here (if any WARN_ON(unexpected events), then handle it accordingly)?",
